               <p xml:id="idm167">"De vilde Jægere" was planned for performance at Gade's concert at Hofteatret (The Court Theatre) on 21 May 1845 but was cancelled for unknown reasons. It was not until February 1847 that it had its first performance. It was included in numerous editions of the Collection of Songs for Male Choir published by Studenter-Sangforeningen.</p>
